<%@ Language="VBScript" CodePage="65001" %><% Response.CharSet="utf-8": pageTitleKo="잉톡 개인정보처리방침": pageTitleEn="Ingtalk Privacy Policy": pageDescriptionKo="잉톡 개인정보처리방침": pageDescriptionEn="Ingtalk Privacy Policy and data practices": currentPage="privacy": currentFile="privacy.asp" %><!--#include file="_header.asp"-->
<main id="main" class="container"><% If lang="en" Then %>
<header class="page-head"><h1>Ingtalk Privacy Policy</h1><p class="effective">Effective: August 23, 2026</p></header><p>Itembus (the “Operator”) publishes this Privacy Policy to explain how personal data is handled securely in the Ingtalk service.</p>
<h2>1. Data and Purposes</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Required profile</td><td>Anonymous user ID, nickname, age or birth year, gender, language, and country</td><td>Create profiles, provide conversation-partner information, and enforce age restrictions</td></tr><tr><td>Service activity</td><td>Talk cards, posts, comments, reactions, chat requests and decisions, messages, reports, and blocks</td><td>Provide the service, resolve disputes, and maintain safety</td></tr><tr><td>Optional data</td><td>Profile and post photos, approximate and precise location</td><td>Display selected photos and provide distance-based discovery</td></tr><tr><td>Device and technical data</td><td>Installation ID, app and OS version, push token, access and error logs</td><td>Restore the device wallet, send notifications, diagnose errors, and prevent abuse</td></tr><tr><td>Purchases and rewards</td><td>Store product, transaction and receipt identifiers, currency, points, and reward history</td><td>Verify purchases, provide points, prevent duplicate rewards, and handle refunds</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Ingtalk does not currently request contacts, microphone access, or permission to track activity across other apps and websites. Advertising-related disclosures will be updated when an advertising SDK is activated.</p>
<h2>2. Retention</h2><ul><li>Active-account profiles and general service data: until account deletion</li><li>User-accessible chat messages: up to 30 days</li><li>Closed support inquiries and error logs: up to 90 days</li><li>Safety message backups and report or enforcement evidence: up to one year</li><li>Device-wallet and repeat-registration prevention records: up to one year after last use or withdrawal</li><li>Records required by law: for the legally required period</li></ul><p>Expired data is irreversibly deleted. Records needed for a legal obligation, investigation, or dispute may be isolated with restricted access until the required period ends. Anonymous board aliases remain linked to internal identifiers where necessary for safety and legal duties.</p>
<h2>3. Service Providers and International Processing</h2><p>The Operator does not sell personal data or disclose it to third parties except with consent or as required by law. The following providers process data on the Operator's behalf.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Location and data</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Supabase, Inc.</td><td>Authentication, database, file storage, realtime services, and server functions</td><td>Accounts, profiles, content, messages, and photos / Seoul, Republic of Korea (ap-northeast-2)</td></tr><tr><td>Expo / 650 Industries, Inc.</td><td>Builds, updates, and push notifications</td><td>App, device, and push-token data / United States and other infrastructure locations</td></tr><tr><td>Functional Software, Inc. (Sentry)</td><td>Error reporting and performance diagnostics</td><td>Error, device, app, and limited user-ID data / United States</td></tr><tr><td>Google Firebase</td><td>Android push delivery</td><td>App identifiers and push-related data / United States and other infrastructure locations</td></tr><tr><td>RevenueCat, Inc. and app stores</td><td>Purchase processing and receipt verification</td><td>User ID, product, transaction, receipt, and currency data / provider infrastructure locations</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>International transfers occur over encrypted networks when a feature is used or an error occurs. Data is retained for the period above or until the processing agreement ends. Users may request restriction or deletion through Support, although this may limit related features.</p>
<h2>4. Location and Optional Permissions</h2><p>Approximate or precise location is used to calculate and display distance ranges. Exact coordinates are not shown to other users. Users can deny location permission and continue using non-location features. Notifications announce chat requests and messages. Only photos explicitly selected through the system picker are processed.</p>
<h2>5. User Rights</h2><p>Users may edit profiles and withdraw permissions under My Info. Accounts and associated data can be deleted under My Info → Delete account. Users can also request access, correction, deletion, restriction, or withdrawal through <a href="<%=LangUrl("deletion.asp")%>">Account &amp; Data Deletion</a>, <a href="mailto:itembus@itembus.com">itembus@itembus.com</a>, or 1555-1645.</p>
<h2>6. Minors</h2><p>Ingtalk is only for users age 19 or older. Accounts and content may be restricted or deleted if use by a minor is identified.</p>
<h2>7. Safeguards and Disposal</h2><p>The Operator applies encryption in transit, database row-level security, separation and auditing of administrative access, reporting, blocking, and account enforcement. Electronic files are deleted in a manner intended to prevent recovery, while legally retained records are kept separately.</p>
<h2>8. Privacy Contact</h2><ul class="contact-list"><li>Privacy officer: Yongil Cho</li><li>Business: Itembus</li><li>Email: <a href="mailto:itembus@itembus.com">itembus@itembus.com</a></li><li>Phone: <a href="tel:15551645">1555-1645</a></li><li>Address: 2F, Suite 215, 4236 Donghae-daero, Sokcho-si, Gangwon State, Republic of Korea</li></ul>
<h2>9. Changes</h2><p>Material changes to this Policy will be announced in the app or on this website before taking effect.</p><h2>10. Remedies</h2><p>Users in the Republic of Korea may contact the Personal Information Infringement Report Center at 118, the Personal Information Dispute Mediation Committee, or another competent authority for advice or dispute resolution.</p>
